%% One valuation run, in order, with the real operations named.
%% Note: avoid "->", angle brackets and semicolons in message text. The
%% lexer reads them as arrow tokens and fails to parse.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant MD as market_data.json
  participant B as bootstrap
  participant QL as GlobalBootstrap
  participant SC as coeffs
  participant GPU as CUDA device
  participant V as reconcile

  MD->>B: 8 curves of tagged quotes

  loop per curve, in dependency order
    B->>B: quote to RateHelper by type
    alt meeting-dated or IMM-dated
      B->>QL: stage 1: ForwardRate + BackwardFlat
      QL-->>B: flat forwards, jumps on policy dates
      B->>B: freeze strip zeros as ZeroPinHelper
      B->>QL: stage 2: pins + long instruments
      QL-->>B: StepSplineCurve, split at tCut
    else single stage
      B->>QL: Discount + LogCubic
      QL-->>B: term structure
    end
    Note over QL: all n pillars solved at once.<br/>A global interpolator has no<br/>bracketing sequential solve
  end

  B->>SC: calibrated term structures
  loop per pillar interval
    SC->>SC: sample logDF, 4 points per interval
    SC->>SC: divided differences give c0..c3
  end
  SC->>GPU: cudaMemcpy CubicCoeffs[]
  Note over SC,GPU: piecewise cubic in logDF,<br/>so the upload is an identity,<br/>not a fit

  par CPU reference path
    B->>V: prices, PV01 re-bootstrapped per bump
  and GPU path
    GPU->>GPU: binary search, then Horner
    GPU->>V: device prices, pillar ladder
  end

  V->>V: difference both paths, 240 instruments
  V-->>MD: worst agreement 3.6e-14
